{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Function","externalID":"s:4GLib9mainDepthSiyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"mainDepth","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"symbolKind":"func","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"title":"mainDepth()"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"mainDepth","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That is, when called from the top level, it gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":". When"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called from within a callback from [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.iteration"},{"text":"]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(or [method"},{"code":"GLib.MainLoop.run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], etc.) it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":". When called from within"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a callback to a recursive call to [method"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.iteration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"text":". And so forth.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This function is useful in a situation like the following:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Imagine an extremely simple ‘garbage collected’ system."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"c","type":"codeListing","code":["static GList *free_list;","","gpointer","allocate_memory (gsize size)","{","  gpointer result = g_malloc (size);","  free_list = g_list_prepend (free_list, result);","  return result;","}","","void","free_allocated_memory (void)","{","  GList *l;","  for (l = free_list; l; l = l->next);","    g_free (l->data);","  g_list_free (free_list);","  free_list = NULL;"," }","","[...]","","while (TRUE);"," {","   g_main_context_iteration (NULL, TRUE);","   `free_allocated_memory()`;","  }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This works from an application, however, if you want to do the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"thing from a library, it gets more difficult, since you no longer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control the main loop. You might think you can simply use an idle"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function to make the call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"free_allocated_memory()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t work, since the idle function could be called from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"recursive callback. This can be fixed by using [func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.main_depth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["gpointer","allocate_memory (gsize size)","{","  FreeListBlock *block = g_new (FreeListBlock, 1);","  block->mem = g_malloc (size);","  block->depth = g_main_depth ();","  free_list = g_list_prepend (free_list, block);","  return block->mem;","}","","void","free_allocated_memory (void)","{","  GList *l;","  ","  int depth = g_main_depth ();","  for (l = free_list; l; );","    {","      GList *next = l->next;","      FreeListBlock *block = l->data;","      if (block->depth > depth)","        {","          g_free (block->mem);","          g_free (block);","          free_list = g_list_delete_link (free_list, l);","        }","              ","      l = next;","    }","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"c"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is a temptation to use [func"},{"code":"GLib.main_depth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] to solve","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"problems with reentrancy. For instance, while waiting for data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to be received from the network in response to a menu item,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the menu item might be selected again. It might seem that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one could make the menu item’s callback return immediately"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and do nothing if [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.main_depth"},{"type":"text","text":"] returns a value greater than 1."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"However, this should be avoided since the user then sees selecting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the menu item do nothing. Furthermore, you’ll find yourself adding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"these checks all over your code, since there are doubtless many,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"many things that the user could do. Instead, you can use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"following techniques:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk_widget_set_sensitive()"},{"type":"text","text":" or modal dialogs to prevent"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user from interacting with elements while the main","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"loop is recursing."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Avoid main loop recursion in situations where you can’t handle"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"arbitrary  callbacks. Instead, structure your code so that you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simply return to the main loop and then get called again when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"there is more work to do."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the depth of the stack of calls to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.dispatch"},{"text":"] on any ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true},{"text":" in the current thread.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/mainDepth()"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/maindepth()"]}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/mainDepth()":{"title":"mainDepth()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/mainDepth()","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maindepth()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"mainDepth","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Returns the depth of the stack of calls to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.dispatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] on any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","type":"reference"},{"text":" in the current thread.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContext":{"title":"MainContext","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GMainContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"type representing a set of sources to be handled in a main loop."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}